[32m+[m[32m## 2. File-by-File Explanation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.1 `acc-connector/app.py`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**What it is:** The main Flask web application — the entry point for everything.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**What it does:**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Serves the entire 4-step wizard UI as an embedded HTML string (no separate template files)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Handles all HTTP routes (`/`, `/connect/acc`, `/callback`, `/hubs`, `/projects`, `/folders`, `/sync`, `/dashboard/data`, etc.)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Manages the Autodesk APS 3-legged OAuth flow (redirects user to Autodesk login, handles the callback, saves tokens)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Manages the Databricks OAuth flow — **currently Azure AD only** (redirects to `login.microsoftonline.com`, exchanges code for token, triggers bootstrap)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Runs bootstrap and sync in background threads so the UI can poll for progress[m
[32m+[m[32m- Implements an in-memory hourly auto-sync scheduler using `threading.Timer`[m
[32m+[m
